  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Documented all 18 Rust unsafe items and all 35 Rust/C FFI boundaries with adjacent contracts; added a fail-closed linked GMP/MPFR version and 64-bit-limb ABI probe; required native GMP and MPFR prefixes to resolve to the exact FLINT dependency archives; added malformed-input, repeated complete-call, and 128-cycle retained-workspace lifecycle tests; regenerated a reproducible receipt with zero documentation gaps. Standard native tests and bridge-instrumented ASan, UBSan, and leak runs pass.",
    "risks": [
      "The sanitizer run instruments the first-party C bridge and test executable, but the prebuilt static FLINT, GMP, MPFR, and OpenBLAS archives are not themselves sanitizer-instrumented.",
      "The safety receipt intentionally leaves generated-source, dependency-license, source-provenance, Miri, and overall production qualification claims false.",
      "The receipt generator retains its legacy sourceRoot label even when invoked with --root packages/class-groups; inventory paths and hashes are package-relative and reproducible.",
      "pnpm test:changed reaches merge:check but correctly rejects stale packages/class-groups/provenance.json hashes; that manifest is outside this lane's claim."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Refresh packages/class-groups/provenance.json hashes in the provenance lane after integration.",
      "Integrate the product-service Cargo change that makes rug/gmp-mpfr-sys use the same system GMP/MPFR domain selected for FLINT, then rerun the ABI and sanitizer tests.",
      "Repeat the native lifecycle and ABI checks on Linux arm64 and macOS arm64; retain the declared Windows fallback until its native dependency route is qualified."
    ]
